  description: A heavily fortified 203mm coastal artillery emplacement designed to
    engage hostile naval vessels at ranges of up to 20 kilometers. Firing conventional
    high-explosive shells, the CD-203 delivers devastating firepower against surface
    targets with increasing accuracy as firing solutions stabilize. Its unguided
    projectiles cannot be intercepted by conventional missile defenses, though the
    emplacement requires direct line of sight and remains vulnerable to airstrikes
    and counter-battery fire.
